  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FW DRR- Disaster and Climate Risk Informed Development in Small Island Development States in Maldives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the country&#x2019;s disaster governance, resilience, and preparedness through a comprehensive approach, aligned with SDG 11 (Sustainable Cities and Communities) and SDG 13 (Climate Action). The project is implemented by UNDP in collaboration with the National Disaster Management Authority (NDMA) and Maldives Meteorological Service (MMS).The project has the following Objectives:1.	Advance disaster and climate-risk-informed development.2.	Strengthen national coordination on early warning systems.3.	Address capacity gaps in disaster and emergency response.4.	Build community and policymaker resilience through capacity building and hazard-specific research.And the following Outputs:1.	Enhanced Disaster Governance2.	Increased Local Capacity3.	Building National Resilience4.	Digitalization of Disaster Preparedness</narrative>
  </description>
